v3.2.16
Radon Player 3.2.16: Steadier DJ and song endings
## 3.2.16: Steadier DJ and song endings (Windows and Android)
- **No more songs skipped after a crossfade:** after a crossfade, the ending song plays on silently in the player while the next one loads. If loading took a while, that song's end counted as the next song ending, so the next song was skipped before you heard it. Only the song really playing counts now.
- **"Ran on past its end" no longer misfires:** the check for a song that keeps going past its end (so Repeat one never gets stuck) compared the next song with the last song's clock while the next was loading, and trusted the player's length even when it was a little short (some MP3s and streams), so it logged nearly every song and could cut one off early. It now only looks at the song really in the player and uses the song's real length. If it ever happens again, Problems says how far in it was and how long the song is.
- **The DJ knows every song you've played:** it could call a song you've played new to you ("you haven't played these yet"), because it matched your plays by the song's full artist ("A & B", "A feat. B") while Last.fm and your imports have it under the lead artist. It now matches the way Most played does, so the plays come from Last.fm and your imports (the plays here only when there are none of those at all), and a song you've ever played in the app is never called new either.
- **Switch it up from your headphones, the reliable way:** pause with your headphones, then Next (a double tap on most earbuds): with the DJ on, it switches it up and starts playing. The quadruple tap (two double taps) didn't work, since earbuds wait after each tap to see if more are coming, so the two Nexts came too far apart and just skipped two songs; it's gone. While playing, Next skips one song as always. The same goes for Next on the lock screen, in the car and on the PC's media keys.
- **Loudness compensation starts off:** on a new install, Loudness compensation (Settings › Sound) is off; the other sound switches stay on from the start. If you've already been using the app, nothing changes for you.

### Good to know
- **Android:** install RadonPlayer.apk over 3.2.15 (same signature, your library and settings stay), or tap Update in Settings.
- **Windows:** Radon-Player-3.2.16.msi installs over 3.2.15, or use Update in Settings.
